config MTK_ION_COMPAT
	bool "Legacy MediaTek /dev/ion ABI on top of DMA-BUF heaps"
	depends on DMABUF_HEAPS && DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM && ARM64
	default n
	help
	  Provides /dev/ion with the handle based ION ABI of the MediaTek
	  4.14 kernel (ALLOC/FREE/MAP/SHARE/IMPORT/SYNC/CUSTOM/HEAP_QUERY)
	  for prebuilt vendor blobs (camera HAL, dpframework). Every legacy
	  heap that is not secure is served by the "system" DMA-BUF heap
	  (or "system-uncached" for uncached requests). Secure/protected
	  heaps are refused. ION_MM_GET_IOVA is served for the M4U
	  camera/MDP region when the DT has a mediatek,mtk-ion-compat-iova
	  node.

	  WARNING: Codec2 (libcodec2_vndk, system and vendor) picks its
	  legacy ION allocator purely because stat("/dev/ion") succeeds and
	  then crashes in client processes (NULL component store). Before
	  enabling this, the ROM must either set debug.c2.use_dmabufheaps=1
	  or label /dev/ion with a type that only the camera HAL may
	  getattr/open (preferably both).

	  The device is only registered when the kernel is booted with

	    mtk_ion_compat.enable=1

	  If unsure, say N.
